(borge-bug (id "BORGE-1783432745")
  (title "iteration 14: deftype prim, dict prims over VStr JSON, render-html prim. Spec gaps surfaced:

1) (deftype 'name 'field1 'field2 ...) primitive registers type_defs on current branch. Spec [storage.types] does not mention the primitive's exact name or argument convention (quoted-symbol args). Implementation choice: all args are quoted symbols so they evaluate to VStr (no DB lookup needed); types live in type_defs.fields as a JSON string array. type_defs is pure metadata; data_rows is shared.

2) Dict prims (dict-get/dict-set/dict-keys) operate on VStr JSON instead of introducing a VDict value type. Spec doesn't mention the dict prims or the JSON-string-as-dict convention. This is a v1 implementation choice that avoids the ripple of adding a new value type (RR in ast.ml value_to_json/of_json, reader, eval). Future plan pass should decide whether to formalize a VDict type or accept the VStr-JSON ergonomic.

3) (render-html STR) primitive: tags the returned VStr with a '__html__:' sentinel prefix that http.ml recognizes and renders RAW (unescaped) into the response. Plain VStr handlers render as bare text in <p>. Other values render pretty-printed in <pre>. Spec [image.htmx-interface] mentions htmx pages but not the render-html primitive or its dispatch conventions. Need planned spec text for: render-html primitive, raw-vs-text-vs-pre dispatch, and the page-shell htmx layout (h1 + content).

4) GET /types system page lists type_defs visible via the recursive-CTE override walk on the current branch. Spec [image.htmx-interface] mentions a type browser but the named routes are not enumerated.

5) Coupled: the existing /bindings, /branches, /binding/<name> pages from it11 are not enumerated as system routes in the spec either. Same gap, same plan pass.

Resolution: track for the next plan-mode pass; no urgent changes needed (all paths are additive over current spec, none contradict it).")
  (status triage)
  (created 2026-07-07)
  (filed-by roerick)
  (doc "")
)
